issue_context.body:
### Description

When using the `System.Text.Json` source generator to serialise properties adorned with `JsonConverterAttribute`, the source generator still generates a default converter for the property type despite this not being used. This causes builds to fail if the property is of a type which `System.Text.Json` does not natively support (in this case `ReadOnlyMemory<byte>`).

### Reproduction Steps

Create a project with these files:

```csharp
// Project.csproj

<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
    <PropertyGroup>
        <OutputType>exe</OutputType>
        <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
        <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    </PropertyGroup>
</Project>

// Program.cs

using System.Text.Json;
using System.Text.Json.Serialization;

var entity = new Entity { Content = new byte[] { 1, 2, 3 } };
var json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(entity, JsonContext.Default.Entity);
Console.WriteLine(json);

record Entity
{
    [JsonConverter(typeof(MemoryConverter))]
    public ReadOnlyMemory<byte> Content { get; set; }
}

[JsonSerializable(typeof(Entity))]
partial class JsonContext : JsonSerializerContext { }

class MemoryConverter : JsonConverter<ReadOnlyMemory<byte>>
{
    public override ReadOnlyMemory<byte> Read(
        ref Utf8JsonReader reader, Type typeToConvert, JsonSerializerOptions options)
    {
        return reader.GetBytesFromBase64();
    }

    public override void Write(
        Utf8JsonWriter writer, ReadOnlyMemory<byte> value, JsonSerializerOptions options)
    {
        writer.WriteBase64StringValue(value.Span);
    }
}
```

Run the project with `dotnet run`.

### Expected behavior

Program should run and output `{"Content":"AQID"}`.

### Actual behavior

Program compilation fails with (full paths redacted):

```
System.Text.Json.SourceGeneration\System.Text.Json.SourceGeneration.JsonSourceGenerator\JsonContext.ReadOnlySpanByte.g.cs(10,129): Error CS0306 : The type 'ReadOnlySpan<byte>' may not be used as a type argument
System.Text.Json.SourceGeneration\System.Text.Json.SourceGeneration.JsonSourceGenerator\JsonContext.ReadOnlySpanByte.g.cs(19,128): Error CS0306 : The type 'ReadOnlySpan<byte>' may not be used as a type argument
System.Text.Json.SourceGeneration\System.Text.Json.SourceGeneration.JsonSourceGenerator\JsonContext.ReadOnlySpanByte.g.cs(14,127): Error CS0306 : The type 'ReadOnlySpan<byte>' may not be used as a type argument
```

### Regression?

No (same behaviour in .NET 7).

### Known Workarounds

- Use reflection serialisation (only if not using AOT)
- Use a different type for the property (in this case `byte[]`), although this may not be an option for other types
- Write a custom `JsonConverter` for the entire class/record

### Configuration

.NET 8.0.100-preview.3.23178.7
Windows 11 x64

